        ],
        "decision_rule": "Worth a drive quote when the valve normally runs well throttled for long hours and most of the head is friction rather than static lift (VSDs suit friction-dominated systems best). Close it if the valve normally runs near fully open, the head is mostly static, or the pump runs few hours.",
        "typical_benefit": {
          "wording": "\"With rotodynamic pump installations, savings of between 30% and 50% have been achieved in many installations by installing VSDs.\" Also: \"It is estimated that 75% of pump systems are oversized, many by more than 20%.\"",
          "source": [
            "S15",
            "S24"
          ],
          "arc": "2.4146 (IAC/ITAC browse page: 5,227 recommendations, 3.0 yr average payback, 31.4% implemented; average dollar figure omitted)",
          "source_titles": [
            "S15: Variable Speed Pumping: A Guide to Successful Applications, Executive Summary (DOE ITP with Europump/HI, DOE/GO-102004-1913, May 2004)",
            "S24: DOE IAC/ITAC database: browse pages, download, schema document"
          ]
        },
        "limits": "On a hand-built model the valve sits on a stream leaving the pump. On an extracted drawing the links have no direction, so the rule takes a control valve within four drawn links that do not pass through other equipment; it may still be on a branch or the suction side, so check the drawing. IAC/ITAC figures are browse-page averages read through a summarizing fetch and not re-verified against the downloadable database; averages are skewed by outliers."
